Arma host packaging for Ubuntu Resolute
======================================

The packaging/ubuntu-resolute branch is the source for the Launchpad
recipe targeting ppa:nmccallum/pichi, resolute only. It contains debian/,
the crates pinned by Cargo.lock in vendor/, and Cargo's complete
.cargo/config.toml, including the burrow, devtree and pmi Git redirects.
LICENSE.dependencies records the bundled crates' licenses and notices.

This branch uses source format 3.0 (native), with version 0.1.0 matching
Cargo.toml. All sources are in one tree. The recipe does not use an orig
tarball or make-orig-source. Build the recipe directly from this branch.

After installing Build-Depends, source and binary builds need no network
or warm Cargo cache. Use /usr/bin/cargo and /usr/bin/rustc on PATH rather
than rustup shims; rust-toolchain.toml pins upstream's development nightly.
From a checkout of this branch, run:

    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc
    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

For a clean Resolute build with a locally configured sbuild chroot:

    sbuild --dist=resolute ../arma_0.1.0.dsc

Bare-metal libraries and linker
-------------------------------

Resolute's main and universe package indexes were checked on 28 October
2026 using apt-cache. They offer libstd-rust-dev and libstd-rust-1.93-dev,
but no Rust bare-metal library packages. Inspection of the amd64 and arm64
libstd-rust-1.93-dev debs (1.93.1+dfsg-0ubuntu6) found only their respective
Linux target libraries, with neither required none target. Therefore this
branch uses cargo, rustc and rust-src >= 1.93 plus lld. Resolute's default
Rust is 1.93.1; use matching compiler and source packages. This is above
arma's 1.88 MSRV to match the distro toolchain and its build-std sources.

Native amd64 builds compile tatu for x86_64-unknown-none. Native arm64
builds compile it for aarch64-unknown-none-softfloat, matching Cargo.toml
and rust-toolchain.toml. The arm64 boot stub must use the softfloat ABI.
Builds are intended for native amd64 and arm64 builders; cross package
builds are rejected.

During every binary build debian/rules runs Cargo -Z build-std=core for
tatu with --offline --locked, compiling core and compiler_builtins from
the installed rust-src. It copies those rlibs into debian/none-sysroot and
passes --sysroot through the selected bare-metal target's RUSTFLAGS.
The subsequent cargo build --offline --locked --release --bin arma
compiles tatu as arma's artifact dependency and embeds it in /usr/bin/arma,
using the private sysroot for tatu and the distro Linux libraries for arma.
Nothing is written into /usr or rust-src. Ubuntu's lld supplies ld.lld.
No clang or compiler-rt C sources are needed by this core-only build.
The distro Rust copyright file is installed as copyright.rust-src.

Both Cargo invocations use private debian/cargo-home and target directories,
CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true and --offline --locked. RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 enables
bindeps and build-std on distro Rust without downloading a nightly.
Global RUSTFLAGS and CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS are unset because they take
precedence over the target-specific sysroot flags. Rust flags supplied by
dpkg-buildflags apply only to the Linux host target.

The clean target removes build output and the private Cargo home and
sysroot. dh_clean excludes vendor/ to preserve checksummed Cargo.toml.orig
files. Package integration tests are skipped because they need burrow,
kernels and network access. Upstream validation still applies before merge.

Refreshing dependencies
-----------------------

On a networked Resolute machine, install Python >= 3.11 and matching cargo,
rustc and rust-src packages. Use the distro tools on PATH, update Cargo.lock
deliberately if needed, then run:

    python3 debian/refresh-vendor.py

The helper runs cargo vendor --locked --versioned-dirs vendor with --sync
for the installed rust-src library workspace. This also vendors dependencies
needed to resolve build-std, even though only core and compiler_builtins
are compiled. It writes .cargo/rust-src.lock, merges the generated crates.io
and Git source redirects with [unstable] bindeps = true and [net] offline =
true, and regenerates LICENSE.dependencies from manifests and supplied
license and notice files. It does not create an orig tarball.

The package build compares .cargo/rust-src.lock with the installed library
lockfile and fails before compilation if they differ. When rust-src changes,
refresh vendor and the source lock together on this branch. Review and
commit vendor/, Cargo.lock, .cargo/config.toml, .cargo/rust-src.lock and
LICENSE.dependencies together. Review upstream changes before updating
this packaging branch. Archive setup and recipe wiring are handled by Infra.

Local validation
----------------

On 28 October 2026, an offline release build passed on Fedora 44 with the
pinned upstream nightly and an initially empty private Cargo home. The
arm64 softfloat tatu build also passed with that toolchain.

A Resolute amd64 base under rootless proot passed dpkg-buildpackage -S
and -b using the distro Rust 1.93.1 toolchain, matching rust-src and lld.
The binary build passed with invalid global Rust flags supplied to verify
that the rules remove them before Cargo runs. Validation used packaged
GNU coreutils for compatibility with proot. All vendored crate checksums
were checked, including after the package clean target.

The Resolute toolchain also built tatu for aarch64-unknown-none-softfloat
offline, first with build-std=core and then with the copied private sysroot.
The arm64 rules were checked with a dry run. A full sbuild and a native
arm64 binary package build were not run. Package integration tests were
skipped for the reasons above.
